{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "introduction",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Visualizing the time-course datasets\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook provides a descriptive view of the datasets shipped with the repository. It focuses on sample size, data quality, population-level dynamics, and single-cell heterogeneity. The plots do not define bursts or test biological hypotheses; they expose structures that can motivate a later modeling or annotation strategy."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "imports-and-style",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "from deeplearning_examples.io import (\n",
    "    load_smad_timecourses,\n",
    "    load_stimulation_timecourses,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "RANDOM_SEED = 42\n",
    "CONDITION_COLORS = {\n",
    "    \"control\": \"#4C78A8\",\n",
    "    \"TGF-beta high\": \"#F58518\",\n",
    "    \"GDF11 high\": \"#54A24B\",\n",
    "    \"stimulation 100 pM\": \"#B279A2\",\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.rcParams.update({\"figure.dpi\": 120, \"axes.spines.top\": False, \"axes.spines.right\": False})"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "inventory-introduction",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Load and inventory\n",
    "\n",
    "The SMAD files contain an explicit time vector and three experimental conditions. The MATLAB files contain trajectories only and are therefore shown against their frame index. Assigning physical time units to those frames would require metadata not stored in the files."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "load-and-summarize",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": "                    trajectories  timepoints  ...  median  maximum\ndataset                                       ...                 \ncontrol                     4478         288  ...   0.469    6.896\nTGF-beta high               2651         288  ...   0.549    8.467\nGDF11 high                  2692         288  ...   0.512    6.180\nstimulation 100 pM           730         289  ...   0.780    4.313\n\n[4 rows x 6 columns]",
      "text/html": "<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>trajectories</th>\n      <th>timepoints</th>\n      <th>missing values</th>\n      <th>minimum</th>\n      <th>median</th>\n      <th>maximum</th>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>dataset</th>\n      <th></th>\n      <th></th>\n      <th></th>\n      <th></th>\n      <th></th>\n      <th></th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th>control</th>\n      <td>4478</td>\n      <td>288</td>\n      <td>0</td>\n      <td>0.069</td>\n      <td>0.469</td>\n      <td>6.896</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>TGF-beta high</th>\n      <td>2651</td>\n      <td>288</td>\n      <td>0</td>\n      <td>0.060</td>\n      <td>0.549</td>\n      <td>8.467</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>GDF11 high</th>\n      <td>2692</td>\n      <td>288</td>\n      <td>0</td>\n      <td>0.056</td>\n      <td>0.512</td>\n      <td>6.180</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>stimulation 100 pM</th>\n      <td>730</td>\n      <td>289</td>\n      <td>0</td>\n      <td>0.090</td>\n      <td>0.780</td>\n      <td>4.313</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>"
     },
     "execution_count": 2,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "smad_data = load_smad_timecourses()\n",
    "stimulation_data = load_stimulation_timecourses()\n",
    "\n",
    "smad_conditions = {\n",
    "    \"control\": smad_data.control,\n",
    "    \"TGF-beta high\": smad_data.tgfb_high,\n",
    "    \"GDF11 high\": smad_data.gdf11_high,\n",
    "}\n",
    "all_datasets = {**smad_conditions, \"stimulation 100 pM\": stimulation_data}\n",
    "\n",
    "def summarize_dataset(name: str, trajectories: np.ndarray) -> dict[str, object]:\n",
    "    finite_values = trajectories[np.isfinite(trajectories)]\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"dataset\": name,\n",
    "        \"trajectories\": trajectories.shape[0],\n",
    "        \"timepoints\": trajectories.shape[1],\n",
    "        \"missing values\": int(np.isnan(trajectories).sum()),\n",
    "        \"minimum\": float(finite_values.min()),\n",
    "        \"median\": float(np.median(finite_values)),\n",
    "        \"maximum\": float(finite_values.max()),\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "dataset_summary = pd.DataFrame(\n",
    "    [summarize_dataset(name, trajectories) for name, trajectories in all_datasets.items()]\n",
    ").set_index(\"dataset\")\n",
    "dataset_summary.round(3)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "dataset-size-plots",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": "<Figure size 1320x432 with 2 Axes>"
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "figure, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(11, 3.6))\n",
    "names = list(all_datasets)\n",
    "colors = [CONDITION_COLORS[name] for name in names]\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[0].bar(names, dataset_summary.loc[names, \"trajectories\"], color=colors)\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel(\"number of trajectories\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(\"Dataset size\")\n",
    "axes[0].tick_params(axis=\"x\", rotation=25)\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[1].bar(names, dataset_summary.loc[names, \"timepoints\"], color=colors)\n",
    "axes[1].set_ylabel(\"number of timepoints\")\n",
    "axes[1].set_title(\"Trajectory length\")\n",
    "axes[1].tick_params(axis=\"x\", rotation=25)\n",
    "\n",
    "figure.tight_layout()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "smad-introduction",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## SMAD conditions\n",
    "\n",
    "The first row shows randomly selected cells and therefore makes cell-to-cell heterogeneity visible. The second row summarizes each population by its median and interquartile range. The latter is more robust to rare high-amplitude events than a mean with a standard deviation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "smad-trajectories",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": "<Figure size 1560x780 with 6 Axes>"
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "rng = np.random.default_rng(RANDOM_SEED)\n",
    "time_hours = smad_data.times / 60.0\n",
    "figure, axes = plt.subplots(2, 3, figsize=(13, 6.5), sharex=True, sharey=\"row\")\n",
    "\n",
    "for column, (name, trajectories) in enumerate(smad_conditions.items()):\n",
    "    color = CONDITION_COLORS[name]\n",
    "    selected = rng.choice(trajectories.shape[0], size=20, replace=False)\n",
    "    axes[0, column].plot(time_hours, trajectories[selected].T, color=color, alpha=0.25, linewidth=0.8)\n",
    "    axes[0, column].set_title(name)\n",
    "\n",
    "    lower, median, upper = np.quantile(trajectories, [0.25, 0.5, 0.75], axis=0)\n",
    "    axes[1, column].fill_between(time_hours, lower, upper, color=color, alpha=0.25, label=\"IQR\")\n",
    "    axes[1, column].plot(time_hours, median, color=color, linewidth=2, label=\"median\")\n",
    "    axes[1, column].set_xlabel(\"time [h]\")\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_ylabel(\"normalized SMAD signal\")\n",
    "axes[1, 0].set_ylabel(\"normalized SMAD signal\")\n",
    "axes[1, 2].legend(frameon=False)\n",
    "axes[0, 0].text(0.01, 0.96, \"20 randomly selected cells\", transform=axes[0, 0].transAxes, va=\"top\")\n",
    "figure.tight_layout()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "feature-introduction",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Descriptive trajectory features\n",
    "\n",
    "The following features compress each trajectory without imposing a burst definition. `baseline` is the median of the first six measurements, corresponding to the first 100 minutes. `peak above baseline` captures amplitude, while temporal standard deviation and mean signal capture variability and sustained activity. These features are correlated and should not be interpreted as independent biological mechanisms."
   ]
  },
